The installed macOS framework Python reports its invocation launcher through
`sys.executable`; the kernel reports the application-bundle interpreter.
The observed distinction agrees with [CPython's framework launcher source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.14.7/Mac/Tools/pythonw.c),
which replaces the process image while preserving the invocation name.
This source-to-observation inference is not a binary-build attestation.

The prospective coordination admission binds invocation and native image paths
and hashes separately. It authenticates ownership before executable admission
so a rejected worker remains terminable; worker readiness precedes the native
image check. See [the qualified scope](../book/src/16dk-inactive-proxy-lifetimes.md).
Actual worker qualification remains separately owned by the execution task.
This observation does not establish the native-proxy startup failure's cause.
